module DASHI.Physics.YangMills.BalabanCMP109LiteralFarRegionFloorQuotientExact where

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ROW A1a, FAR REGION:  A POINTWISE DENOMINATOR FLOOR FROM A *SINGLE*
--   AXIS, AND THE QUOTIENT BOUND IT GIVES.
--
-- PRIMARY SOURCES
--
-- Kenneth G. Wilson, "Confinement of quarks", Physical Review D 10 (1974),
-- 2445--2459.  DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevD.10.2445.
--
-- Tadeusz Bałaban, "Renormalization Group Approach to Lattice Gauge Field
-- Theories. I.", Communications in Mathematical Physics 109 (1987), 249--301.
-- DOI: 10.1007/BF01215223.
--
-- THE DEFECT THIS MODULE REMOVES.
--
-- `BalabanCMP109LiteralLatticeInversePropagatorExact` bounds the literal
-- lattice inverse propagator below by `sum_mu 4 l_mu^2` from a table of
-- per-axis lower bounds `l_mu` on the sine atoms.  That is a *syntactic*
-- derivation in the bound calculus, so the table must be one and the same at
-- every point of the region.
--
-- On the far region of a near/far split that table does not exist, and this
-- is not a technical inconvenience but the structure of the region: off the
-- coordinate box `{ p : |p_mu| <= r for all mu }` all one knows is that
-- *some* axis has `|p_mu| > r`, and *which* axis it is varies from point to
-- point.  Every per-axis lower bound valid at every far point is therefore
-- zero, and the syntactic route yields no floor at all.
--
-- The fix is to leave the syntactic calculus for this step and work with the
-- exact semantics pointwise, where "some axis" is exactly what one can use:
-- the inverse propagator is a sum of four nonnegative terms, so a single
-- large axis already floors it.
--
-- WHAT IS PROVED HERE:
--
--   * `hatSquaredValueFloorFromAxis` -- if at a point *one* axis has
--     `sigma <= |sin(p_mu/2)|` with `sigma >= 0`, then the literal inverse
--     propagator value at that point is at least `4 sigma^2`.  No assumption
--     whatsoever on the other three axes.
--   * `flooredQuotient` -- the far-region counterpart of the Ward-compensated
--     near estimate: a literal quotient whose numerator has modulus at most
--     `S` and whose denominator is at least `f > 0` obeys `|z| * f <= S`,
--     pointwise, by inversion of the exact semantics.  This is the honest
--     `S / f` bound, and it is where the floor is paid for.
--   * `flooredModulusBound`, `flooredNegativePart` -- the two consumer forms.
--   * `FarRegionOrbit` and `flooredCombinedNegativePart` -- the (4,6,4,1)
--     weighted far-region density bound, i.e. the far half of the
--     `combinedLower` hypothesis of the cancellation-preserving gate, in the
--     same shape as the near half.
--   * Section 4 -- the numbers.  With the repository's own constructive outer
--     Brillouin sine gap `|sin| >= 87/128`
--     (`BalabanBishopOuterBrillouinSineGapExact`) the floor is `7569/4096`,
--     so a unit numerator sup gives a far density bound of `4096/7569 < 1`.
--     That is far inside the far budget `25/4` which the split-parameter
--     optimisation at `r = 2/5`
--     (`BalabanCMP109LiteralOneLoopBoxNearFarOptimisationExact`) allows, and
--     the module machine-checks the comparison.
--
-- WHAT IS STILL OPEN.  The bridge from the far region of the momentum split
-- to the per-point single-axis sine bound `sigma` -- that is, that off the
-- box some coordinate really does have `|sin(p_mu/2)| >= sigma` -- is a
-- trigonometric statement about the valuation, not proved here; and so is the
-- numerator sup `S` of the literal joint Wilson + reduced Faddeev--Popov +
-- Haar numerator on that region.
--
-- Exact rational arithmetic; no postulate, no hole, no receipt, no pragma.
-- Checked with `agda --safe`.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

